c(6,'prompt','In an idealised timing oracle, each additional matching hex character is distinguishable and the secret 32-character tag remains fixed. Ignoring repetitions and noise, roughly how many candidate choices does a position-by-position search use, versus the full tag space?','Specifiedtoyassumptions.')
c(6,'workedExample','The full tag space has 16^32 = 2^128 possibilities. In the stipulated prefix oracle, up to 16 candidate choices at each of 32 positions gives roughly 512 choices. Real measurements can require many repetitions or may not expose this signal at all. This arithmetic is not a network timing-attack benchmark.','Limittoyoracle.')
c(8,'explanation','An HS256 JWS carries base64url-encoded readable claims; it is signed, not encrypted. JWTs can also use JWE encryption, so this is not true of every JWT form.','JWTcanencrypted.',['https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519'],0)
c(8,'text','A compromised service holding the shared key can create tags for arbitrary JWT claims accepted under that key','Otherclaimchecksneednotanyuseraccepted.',option=2)
c(9,'prompt','Assume suitable random independent keys, fresh unpredictable CBC IVs, unambiguous encoding and required replay controls. Which encryption/MAC composition best protects ciphertext and IV integrity before decryption?','OriginalsecuremissingCBCIV/protocolassumptions.')
c(9,'workedExample','Encrypt with a suitable fresh unpredictable CBC IV and key k1. Authenticate the IV, ciphertext and relevant context using independent k2 and an unambiguous encoding. Reject invalid tags before decryption. Replay and key-management requirements remain separate. Prefer a maintained AEAD implementation when available.','Ordernotcompleteprotocol.')
c(11,'prompt','A link uses a 32-bit truncated HMAC tag. Assume a fixed valid context with no expiry, independent random tag guesses with replacement, and 1,000 verification attempts per second. What is the expected waiting time for success?','Geometricexpectationrequiresreplacement/infinitewindow.')
c(11,'workedExample','Each independent guess succeeds with probability 2^-32, so mean waiting time is 2^32 attempts. At 1,000/s this is about 49.7 days; the 50% success time is shorter, about 34.5 days. This assumes the same accepted context and no expiry or rate limit. Choose tag length and lifetime from the forgery budget; a random server-side token also requires sufficient entropy and request limits.','Meanmedianandrandomtokennotmagicsolution.')
c(12,'workedExample','HMAC-SHA256, keyed BLAKE2b and KMAC256 are specified keyed constructions. SHA256(k || msg) admits length extension, and SHA256(msg) has no authentication key. Needing a key and resisting extension are necessary considerations here, not a general proof that any other candidate MAC is sound.','Noextensionnotsecurityproof.')
